cbmp: libraries poll the interrupt request in long C loops (Lua 5.4.7).
lstrlib: match() steps, singlematch and %f (weighted by class length), back-references
(weighted by capture length), %b scan and lmemfind (weighted by needle length) poll every
4096 work units; string.rep of empty pieces returns "" at once and string.rep builds its
result by doubling (O(log n) copies, polling between them). ltablib: insert/remove/
move/concat per iteration and every sort comparison. loslib: os.date per conversion.
Re-check on upgrade: MatchState, match, singlematch, match_capture, matchbalance, lmemfind,
prepstate, str_rep; tinsert/tremove/tmove/tconcat/sort_comp; os_date.

